  "body": "U4 of the tool library redesign (#3663). The Tool tab of the tool library window gets an assembly group. In the group, a user sets the holder, the gauge length and the stick-out (projection) of a tool.\n\n## What changed\n- New `tool_library_dialog/assembly_group.rs`. It shows:\n  - the holder pick, the gauge length and the projection (the same fields as the shape window, from `tool_holder_picker::holder_fields`);\n  - the read-only total gauge length (gauge length plus projection);\n  - the `fits_shank` refusal by name;\n  - a warning when the holder taper is not the `tooling.spindle_mount` of the machine;\n  - what Apply holder would refuse (for example, a nose in the flutes), before the click. This refusal is judged on the stored tool, as `SetToolBody::library` judges it;\n  - a separate \"Draft note\" when the unapplied tool numbers do not take the holder, but the stored tool does;\n  - a note when a tool length change re-seeded the projection.\n- Apply holder is the existing `SetToolBody::library`: one undo step. No new command. No MCP tool is owed.\n- The window keeps its own holder draft (`ToolEditorView::holder`). `with_library_draft` swaps it into `tool_profile_ui`, as U2 does for `tool_ui`. The drafts of the window and of the shape window do not mix.\n- #808 item 2: when the flute length plus the shank length of the stored tool changes, the projection draft takes the new stick-out and is marked (`ToolProfileUi::reseeded`). The stored `HolderRef` changes only on Apply holder.\n- The preview draws the draft holder. It uses the same path as the command (`resolve`, `fits_shank`, `tool_body::build_library`, `tool_body::fits`), in the memo of the preview, so a still frame builds nothing. A refused pick keeps the landed body. The stick-out of a library holder is its stated projection.\n- `tool_holder_picker` is split into `holder_fields` and `apply_holder_button`. The shape window draws the two as before.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3895-tool-holder-group.md`.\n\nHeld back to #3930 (see the decision file): the Properties summary page, the picker removal from the shape window, and the Body section in the window. Each of these items moves many tests or needs a body draft that belongs to the window.\n\n## Readings\n- EM-0600-4FL with BT30 ER20, projection 70: the preview shows stick-out 70.00 and gauge 130.00. The total shows 130.00 mm.\n- ER20 chuck applied at projection 55, then shank length 40 to 50: the draft projection is 65, marked. The stored `HolderRef` projection stays 55 until Apply holder.\n- BT30 Weldon 12 mm on the 8 mm shank: \"a Ø8.000 mm shank does not fit - the holder takes a Ø12.000 mm shank\" before the click. Apply holder is refused by name (\"holder not set: ...\"). Nothing lands.\n\n## Pinning tests\nNew in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_assembly.rs`:\n- `apply_holder_is_one_set_tool_body`\n- `a_shank_the_holder_cannot_take_is_warned`\n- `a_projection_in_the_flutes_is_named_before_apply`\n- `a_tool_length_change_reseeds_the_projection_draft_only`\n- `the_window_holder_draft_and_the_shape_window_do_not_mix`\n- `the_refusal_judges_the_stored_tool_not_shorter_draft_flutes` (review fix: draft flutes 5 mm, stored 15 mm, ER20 chuck at projection 10 - the refusal shows and Apply holder refuses)\n- `longer_draft_flutes_give_a_draft_note_not_an_apply_refusal` (review fix: draft flutes 25 mm, projection 20 - no refusal, a draft note, and Apply holder lands)\n\nUpdated: `page_layout_tool_library::layout_window_tool_editor` asserts the assembly group under the geometry rows.\n\nThe `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes from 1789 to 1796. No test is deleted. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Gate of the review fix (macOS, head 9af86ad9f)\n- The two new tests failed before the fix (the stored-tool refusal was empty; a false refusal on the draft flutes) and pass after it.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 18 steps, 18 ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 3.3 min. ui lib: 1615 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: exit 0.\n- The head merges cleanly with origin/main (`git merge-tree`).\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild, head 28fc33a2a merged with origin/main)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: dry run 18 steps; run 18 ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 6.7 min (ui build, ui lib, 16 ui suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: exit 0.\n- No heavy step: this issue is P4, not P1. No post or toolpath changed, so no `example_catalog*` suite applies. The light lane was not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n- A click on \"Apply holder\" inside the scroll area of the window: the tests queue the same call through `with_library_draft`, because the button can be below the fold of the test screen.\n- The taper warning against a machine with a `tooling.spindle_mount`: drawn, not pinned by a test.\n\n## Screenshots (headless, winbuild)\nBefore (origin/main), Tool tab: no holder group.\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3895/before-tool-tab.png)\n\nAfter: BT30 ER20 draft at projection 70; the preview shows stick-out 70 and gauge 130.\n![after holder draft](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3895/after-holder-draft.png)\n\nAfter: a holder that the shank does not fit is named before Apply.\n![after shank warning](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3895/after-shank-warning.png)\n\nAfter: a tool length change re-seeds the projection draft only.\n![after reseed](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3895/after-reseed.png)\n\nChangelog: Set a tool's holder, gauge length and stick-out in the tool library window. The stick-out follows a change of tool length before you apply the holder.\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #808\nFixes #3895\n\n",
